EVALUATION.md §9.3, TYPES.md §1, DECISIONS 185: an active layer with a static error (E2102) is
broken; the let it amends is poisoned without a finding. Layers apply in order: `one` takes the
sound layer, then is poisoned; `three`'s earlier layer fails first (E1905, reported), so the
broken layer never runs; `four` is poisoned by the broken layer, so the later layer's failing
amendment never runs (no E1905); `two` only sound layers amend, and is amended normally.
-- layers --
first good bad last
-- a/a.canon --
/// A.
package a

/// Rarity.
enum Rarity { common, rare }

/// An item.
record Item {
  /// Its rarity.
  rarity: Rarity = common
  /// Its weight.
  weight: Int = 1
  /// Its limits.
  limits: {String: [Int]} = { "a": [1] }
}

/// One.
let one: Item = {}

/// Two.
let two: Item = {}

/// Three.
let three: Item = {}

/// Four.
let four: Item = {}
-- a/first.canon --
package a
layer first

amend three {
  limits["zz"][0]: 2
}
-- a/good.canon --
package a
layer good

amend one {
  weight: 2
}

amend two {
  weight: 3
}
-- a/bad.canon --
package a
layer bad

amend one {
  rarity: legendary
}

amend three {
  weight: 4
}

amend four {
  weight: 5
}
-- a/last.canon --
package a
layer last

amend four {
  limits["zz"][0]: 3
}
-- dump.txt --
a.one poisoned
a.two = Item{rarity: common, weight: 3, limits: {"a": [1]}}
a.three poisoned
a.four poisoned

error[E2102]  a/bad.canon:5:11
  unknown name legendary

error[E1905]  a/first.canon:5:9
  three: amend path limits["zz"][0]: key zz does not exist

2 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
